{"units": [{"id": "pleion-note5", "translation": "Thus Casaubon for οὐ [not]"}, {"id": "pleion-note6", "translation": "in all which places πλέον [more] seems to be restored. The remaining examples of Aeschylus are these:"}, {"id": "pleion-note7", "translation": "Σχολὴ δὲ [But leisure]"}, {"id": "pleion-note8", "translation": "Εἰ στράτευμα [If an army]"}, {"id": "pleion-note9", "translation": "unless πλεῖον ἢ [more than] was introduced from a gloss for πληθύοι [should be full], about which I have spoken in the Preface to the fifth Leipzig edition p. LXIX."}, {"id": "pleion-note10", "translation": "Δέρκεται [He sees]"}, {"id": "pleion-note11", "translation": "Οἴκῳ καὶ πόλει [For house and city]"}, {"id": "pleion-note12", "translation": "Εἰ γάρ τι κακῶν ἄκος οἶδε [For if he knows any remedy for evils]"}, {"id": "pleion-note13", "translation": "Καὶ [And]"}, {"id": "pleion-note14", "translation": "in the verse of an interpolator"}, {"id": "pleion-note15", "translation": "Ἐξεύχεται τὸ δρᾶμα τοῦ πάθους [The drama of suffering prays for]"}, {"id": "pleion-note16", "translation": "Πλέον [More]"}, {"id": "pleion-note17", "translation": "Εἶργε μὴ [Prevent from]"}, {"id": "pleion-note18", "translation": "Τὸ δ᾽ εὐτυχεῖν, τόδ᾽ ἐν βροτοῖσι θεός τε καὶ θεοῦ [But to prosper, this among mortals is god and more than god]"}, {"id": "pleion-note19", "translation": "Ὅρκος γὰρ οὔτι Ζηνὸς ἰσχύει [For the oath of Zeus has no strength]"}, {"id": "pleion-note20", "translation": "Τὸ δυσσεβές γὰρ ἔργον μετὰ μὲν [For the impious deed after]"}, {"id": "pleion-note21", "translation": "Πάθη ὁρῶσα [Seeing suffering]"}, {"id": "pleion-note22", "translation": "Καλῶς τὰ [Well the]"}, {"id": "pleion-note23", "translation": "Οὐ τοῦτο δειμαίνεις [Do you not fear this]"}, {"id": "pleion-note24", "translation": "Θαυμάσει [He will marvel]"}, {"id": "pleion-note25", "translation": "Τὸν πε-σόντα λακτίσαι [To kick the fallen]"}, {"id": "pleion-note26", "translation": "Ὡς [As]"}, {"id": "pleion-note27", "translation": "Ἀβρύνεται γὰρ πᾶς τις εὐ πράσσων [For everyone who fares well becomes delicate]"}, {"id": "pleion-note28", "translation": "Ἁπαντας ἐχθροὺς τῶν θεῶν ἡγοῦ [Consider all enemies of the gods]"}, {"id": "pleion-note29", "translation": "Κρατοῦντες τὸ πᾶν δίκας [Ruling all justice]"}, {"id": "pleion-note30", "translation": "which he called πέρα δίκης [beyond justice] in Prom. 30, whence here too Heimsoeth conjectured δίκας πέρα [beyond justice] p. 103, comparing Hesychius who explains πέρα [beyond] by πλέον [more]."}, {"id": "pleion-note31", "translation": "Διδαχθεὶς ἂν τόδ᾽ εἰδείην [Having been taught, I would know this]"}, {"id": "pleion-note32", "translation": "Τὸ σωφρονεῖν τιμῶσα τοῦ βίου [Honoring prudence more than life]"}, {"id": "pleion-note33", "translation": "Σὺ δ᾽ οὖν δίωκε καὶ πόνον [But you pursue also toil]"}, {"id": "pleion-note34", "translation": "where Auratus conjectured πλέω [more], which should have been πλείω [more]. Heimsoeth here too πέρα [beyond]. Perhaps πόνου [of toil] should be written. On restoring πλέον [more] in three verses of Agamemnon see under πλείων [more]."}, {"id": "pleion-quote1", "translation": "to say more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote2", "translation": "having thrown more, I will be dishonored"}, {"id": "pleion-quote3", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote4", "translation": "more than I wish is present to me"}, {"id": "pleion-quote5", "translation": "more than the Median"}, {"id": "pleion-quote6", "translation": "something more than what has been revealed"}, {"id": "pleion-quote7", "translation": "more evil"}, {"id": "pleion-quote8", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote9", "translation": "more than \"alas\" indeed"}, {"id": "pleion-quote10", "translation": "burning more than what has been said"}, {"id": "pleion-quote11", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote12", "translation": "hatred"}, {"id": "pleion-quote13", "translation": "to bear more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote14", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote15", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote16", "translation": "produces more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote17", "translation": "more than the time of sleeping together"}, {"id": "pleion-quote18", "translation": "more war comes from the gods"}, {"id": "pleion-quote19", "translation": "more?"}, {"id": "pleion-quote20", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote21", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote22", "translation": "to be bold more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote23", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote24", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote25", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote26", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote27", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-quote28", "translation": "consider more"}, {"id": "pleion-word1", "translation": "much"}, {"id": "pleion-word2", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word3", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word4", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word5", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word6", "translation": "of more, to more"}, {"id": "pleion-word7", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word8", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word9", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word10", "translation": "of more, more, more"}, {"id": "pleion-word11", "translation": "This man has been wounded by the net"}, {"id": "pleion-word12", "translation": "Not indeed"}, {"id": "pleion-word13", "translation": "There is no escape, strangers, in time"}, {"id": "pleion-word14", "translation": "not"}, {"id": "pleion-word15", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word16", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word17", "translation": "But leisure"}, {"id": "pleion-word18", "translation": "If an army"}, {"id": "pleion-word19", "translation": "more than"}, {"id": "pleion-word20", "translation": "should be full"}, {"id": "pleion-word21", "translation": "He sees"}, {"id": "pleion-word22", "translation": "For house and city"}, {"id": "pleion-word23", "translation": "For if he knows any remedy for evils"}, {"id": "pleion-word24", "translation": "And"}, {"id": "pleion-word25", "translation": "The drama of suffering prays for"}, {"id": "pleion-word26", "translation": "More"}, {"id": "pleion-word27", "translation": "Prevent from"}, {"id": "pleion-word28", "translation": "But to prosper, this among mortals is god and more than god"}, {"id": "pleion-word29", "translation": "For the oath of Zeus has no strength"}, {"id": "pleion-word30", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word31", "translation": "For the impious deed after"}, {"id": "pleion-word32", "translation": "Seeing suffering"}, {"id": "pleion-word33", "translation": "the more"}, {"id": "pleion-word34", "translation": "Well the"}, {"id": "pleion-word35", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word36", "translation": "Do you not fear this"}, {"id": "pleion-word37", "translation": "He will marvel"}, {"id": "pleion-word38", "translation": "To kick the fallen"}, {"id": "pleion-word39", "translation": "As"}, {"id": "pleion-word40", "translation": "For everyone who fares well becomes delicate"}, {"id": "pleion-word41", "translation": "Consider all enemies of the gods"}, {"id": "pleion-word42", "translation": "Ruling all justice"}, {"id": "pleion-word43", "translation": "beyond justice"}, {"id": "pleion-word44", "translation": "beyond justice"}, {"id": "pleion-word45", "translation": "beyond"}, {"id": "pleion-word46", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word47", "translation": "Having been taught, I would know this"}, {"id": "pleion-word48", "translation": "Honoring prudence more than life"}, {"id": "pleion-word49", "translation": "But you pursue also toil"}, {"id": "pleion-word50", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word51", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word52", "translation": "beyond"}, {"id": "pleion-word53", "translation": "of toil"}, {"id": "pleion-word54", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "pleion-word55", "translation": "more"}, {"id": "plektanao-orth1", "translation": "to entangle like tendrils"}, {"id": "plektanao-def1", "translation": "or πλεκτανów I entangle like tendrils."}, {"id": "plektanao-note1", "translation": "Πεπλεκτανημέναι [Entangled]"}, {"id": "plektanao-note2", "translation": "The more probable form is πεπλεκτανωμέναι [entangled], restored by Schneider, which is read in Hippocr. p. 279, 118. ἔστι δὲ πολύρριζος διὰ τοῦ ἥπατος πεπλεκτανωμένη [It is many-rooted, entangled through the liver]."}, {"id": "plektanao-quote1", "translation": "with dense serpents"}, {"id": "plektanao-word1", "translation": "tendril"}, {"id": "plektanao-word2", "translation": "Entangled"}, {"id": "plektanao-word3", "translation": "entangled"}, {"id": "plektanao-word4", "translation": "It is many-rooted, entangled through the liver"}, {"id": "plektane-orth1", "translation": "coil"}, {"id": "plektane-def1", "translation": "coil."}, {"id": "plektane-def2", "translation": "siphon."}, {"id": "plektane-note1", "translation": "Ὄφεων δὲ πλε-κτάναισι περίδρομον κύτος [A vessel surrounded by coils of serpents]"}, {"id": "plektane-note2", "translation": "Μίαν παρείρας [Having inserted one]"}]}